<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The window themes, so a cold start does not flash before Compose draws.

  The platform default this replaced (@android:style/Theme.Material.NoActionBar)
  has a window background that is not the app's ground, which meant a light flash
  on the launch path of a dark privacy app, every time.

  P2-23 makes it two: the app has a light scheme now, and a light-mode user given
  the dark ground gets exactly the flash this style exists to prevent, in the other
  direction.

  **No values-night variant, and the reason changed.** It used to be that DESIGN.md
  §3 made the app dark-only and a night variant would imply there was a day one.
  Now there is a day one — but a values-night qualifier resolves from the *system's*
  night-mode flag, and the setting is System/Light/Dark. A user who forced Light on a
  dark-system phone is exactly who cares, and a qualifier would hand them the dark
  ground on every launch. MainActivity picks the theme with setTheme() before
  super.onCreate, which is early enough for windowBackground and reads the app's own
  preference rather than the platform's.

  AppCompatDelegate.setDefaultNightMode is the usual way to do this and is not
  available: androidx.appcompat is not on this project's classpath, and adding a
  Gradle dependency plus an I1 clearance run to set a window background is not a
  trade worth making.

  P2-6 removed four items from this style: statusBarColor, navigationBarColor,
  windowLightStatusBar and windowLightNavigationBar. All four are no-ops at
  targetSdk 37 — Android 15 stopped honouring the bar colours under enforced
  edge-to-edge — and a no-op that reads like configuration is how the next
  person concludes bar colour is handled somewhere. The bars are transparent and
  the app draws its own ground behind them; their *icon* colours are set in code
  by enableEdgeToEdge, from the resolved scheme (P2-23). `DesignTokensTest` fails
  if any of the four returns.

  windowBackground stays: it is what actually prevents the cold-start flash, and
  it is unaffected by edge-to-edge.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.Vault" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/vault_ground</item>
        <item name="android:colorBackground">@color/vault_ground</item>
    </style>

    <style name="Theme.Vault.Light" parent="Theme.Vault">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/vault_ground_light</item>
        <item name="android:colorBackground">@color/vault_ground_light</item>
    </style>
</resources>
